8. Duties of a practitioner

A practitioner who reasonably suspects that a person under his or her care is a victim of domestic violence shall assist the victim in the following manner—
(a)	offer the requisite medical assistance to the victim;
(b)	accurately document the visit of the victim;
(c)	inform the victim of options available within the judicial system to the victim; or
(d)	make himself or herself available to testify in court regarding the case where necessary.

